{"title":"1984 IMO Problems/Problem 5","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1984_IMO_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/a/96ab646de7704969b91c76a214126b45f2b07b25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> be the sum of the lengths of all the diagonals of a plane convex polygon with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> vertices (where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/d/70d8a348130d140aad5a9c23958578539f753241.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n&gt;3$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"43\" height=\"13\" />). Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> be its perimeter. Prove that:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/9/a/59a9cef9ad189f08f3a0fa70b1523eccef98ea1a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[n-3&lt;{2d\\over p}&lt;\\Bigl[{n\\over2}\\Bigr]\\cdot\\Bigl[{n+1\\over 2}\\Bigr]-2,\\]\" width=\"256\" height=\"41\" />\nwhere <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/e/bceb7b14e55d33a8bca29b7863ad3cdae95afce4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[x]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"18\" height=\"18\" /> denotes the greatest integer not exceeding <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1984_IMO_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Consider all the pairs of non-adjacent sides in the polygon. Each pair uniquely determines two diagonals which intersect in an interior point. The sum of these two diagonals is greater than the sum of the two sides (triangle inequality). Each side will appear in a pair <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/5/31503c8c86ff405ea9ae2dd6285eecb04550cb97.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n-3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"44\" height=\"15\" /> times. And each time the side appears it also includes two diagonals. Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/e/66e1f0f279613410eeb4f1ad8416efddca23b48f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(n-3)p &lt; 2d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"108\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>Note that for any diagonal, its length is less than the sum of the sides on either side of it (triangle inequality). Consider all the diagonals from a fixed vertex and using the least number of sides in each application of the triangle inequality. We can sum everything up over all the diagonals considering the two cases (even or odd) to get the result.\n</p><p>This solution was posted and copyrighted by aznlord1337. The original thread for this problem can be found here: <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external autonumber\" href=\"https://aops.com/community/p1389256\">[1]</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"clear:both; margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1984_IMO\" title=\"1984 IMO\">1984 IMO</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1984_IMO_Problems\" title=\"1984 IMO Problems\">Problems</a></b>) • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c3222\">Resources</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1984_IMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1984 IMO Problems/Problem 4\">Problem 4</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"34%\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1984_IMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1984 IMO Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1984_IMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1984 IMO Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1984_IMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1984 IMO Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1984_IMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1984 IMO Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1984_IMO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1984 IMO Problems/Problem 6\">6</a>\n</td>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1984_IMO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1984 IMO Problems/Problem 6\">Problem 6</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=IMO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"IMO Problems and Solutions\"> All IMO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261016233916\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.020 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.033 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 73/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 895/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 44/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 1616/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTrans